kindHolderT -- PLUS-EQUALS ON A HOLDER, INTERPRETED ROAD. Minted 2026-09-25 for
Tony's ruling that the refusal stands: checkOP asks getDataType for the
receiver's kind name, and getDataType refuses on a field that holds a group.

kH is made a holder of kN, then plus-equals fires on it twice. Each fire, between
its MARK pair, must print exactly one getDataType refusal (once per fire, by its
text) and then opPlusEQ's own answer, its default arm, which names itself
"ERROR Operator += failed". Nothing is written: holder and source both stay 5.

The jitted road is kindHolderJitT, a separate process by bear-trap 25.
